# ============================================================================
# EGBaccloria — Public Frontend Environment Variables (Safe for Client Bundle)
# ============================================================================
# SECURITY RULES:
# 1. NEVER put `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` or Firebase Admin service-account keys in
#    this file or any `VITE_*` variable! Anything prefixed with `VITE_` is
#    bundled into browser JavaScript.
# 2. Store `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` exclusively in Firebase Secret Manager:
#      npx firebase-tools functions:secrets:set OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#
# The Firebase web config (apiKey, authDomain, projectId, ...) lives in
# `src/services/firebase.ts`. Those values are public identifiers, not secrets;
# access is enforced by Firebase Auth + `firestore.rules`.
# ============================================================================

# Optional: URL of the deployed `openrouterTts` Cloud Function (shown after
# `npx firebase-tools deploy --only functions`). Leave unset to use the
# built-in Web Speech voices only.
# VITE_FIREBASE_TTS_FUNCTION_URL=https://us-central1-your-project-id.cloudfunctions.net/openrouterTts

# ============================================================================
# Google Sign-In Configuration Notes (Firebase Console):
# - Authentication -> Sign-in method -> enable "Google".
# - Authentication -> Settings -> Authorized domains -> add:
#     localhost
#     <your-github-username>.github.io   (or your custom production domain)
# ============================================================================
